{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And he cried, etc., saying.</b> The reason he said <b>saying</b> is that it comes with an explanation, so that they would not say that he was resentful and they would hold him as bearing a grudge, and the words of Aaron would tell them — therefore he said in his crying to HaShem so that they would not say the things stated nearby from the mouth of Aaron:" "<b>Further,</b> it intends that he said before HaShem, prior to his prayer, that he forgives the insult to his honor, and afterwards he prayed ״אֵל נָא״ etc.:" "<b>El na.</b> He intended to ask from the attribute of kindness, as it says (Psalms 52:3) ״חֶסֶד אֵל״. נָא — an expression of request and entreaty, to arouse mercy. <b>Refa na</b> — meaning now, and let it not be delayed."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:11.653068263Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}